  "summary": "Keyword co-occurrence in networking/orchestrator code; no traced installer harm",
  "details": "Package ships SDK code for room/server orchestration and region routing. Static keyword patterns matched on the co-occurrence of `curl`, `ping`, `POST`, and `GET` tokens across bin/room-orchestrator-boot.js, src/sdk/RoomOrchestrator.js, src/sdk/ServerAPI.js, and src/sharding/RegionRouter.js — the shape expected for a networking SDK that performs health checks (ping/latency measurement for region routing) and HTTP requests to a server API. No hardcoded attacker-controlled destination, credential-path read (`~/.aws`, `~/.ssh`, `~/.npmrc`), environment scraping, wallet/browser-secret enumeration, dropper, or install-time lifecycle execution is present in the cited evidence. The `curl` references appear in a bin-invoked orchestrator boot script rather than an install lifecycle hook, and the `ping`/`POST`/`GET` references are consistent with the package's documented networking role.",
